---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import OceanMap from '../components/OceanMap.astro';
import TrendChart from '../components/TrendChart.astro';
import ForecastChart from '../components/ForecastChart.astro';
import DataNotice from '../components/DataNotice.astro';
import { env } from 'cloudflare:workers';
import { getData } from '../lib/data';
import { formatDate, seasonLabel, signed } from '../lib/enso';
import { ArrowUpRight, ArrowRight, Activity, WavesHorizontal as Waves, CalendarDays, Check } from '@lucide/astro';
const { snapshot, stale } = await getData(env);
const weekly = snapshot.weekly.data.at(-1)!;
const priorWeek = snapshot.weekly.data.at(-2)!;
const roni = snapshot.roni.data.at(-1)!;
const discussion = snapshot.discussion.data;
const target = snapshot.forecast.data.rows.find(row => row.season === 'DJF') ?? snapshot.forecast.data.rows[0];
---
<Layout title="ENSO Tracker & Seasonal Outlook" active="overview">
  <div class="page-shell">
    <div class="page-intro"><div><div class="eyebrow intro-eyebrow"><span class="live-dot"></span> THE ENSO OBSERVATORY</div><h1>A clearer view of <span>ENSO.</span></h1><p>The ocean signal. The seasonal outlook. The context that matters.</p></div><div class="snapshot-stamp"><CalendarDays size={15} /><div><strong>{formatDate(discussion.issued)}</strong><span>CPC discussion issued</span></div></div></div>
    <DataNotice stale={stale} />
    <section class="status-band" aria-label="Official ENSO snapshot">
      <div class="phase-stat"><div class="stat-label"><Activity size={14} /> OFFICIAL STATUS</div><div class="phase-value"><span class="phase-dot" style={{ background: discussion.phase === 'El Niño' ? '#d77655' : discussion.phase === 'La Niña' ? '#6c96ae' : '#77807a' }}></span>{discussion.phase}<span class="phase-badge">{discussion.alert}</span></div><p>CPC discussion · {formatDate(discussion.issued)}</p></div>
      <div class="numeric-stat"><div class="stat-label">WEEKLY NIÑO 3.4</div><div class="stat-value">{signed(weekly.anomaly)}<span>°C</span></div><p><span class="change-pill">{signed(weekly.anomaly - priorWeek.anomaly)}°C</span> · {formatDate(weekly.date)}</p></div>
      <div class="numeric-stat"><div class="stat-label">SEASONAL RONI</div><div class="stat-value">{signed(roni.value)}<span>°C</span></div><p>{seasonLabel(roni)} · three-month index <a href="/methodology/#indices" aria-label="Learn about the seasonal RONI index"><ArrowUpRight size={13} /></a></p></div>
      <div class="outlook-stat"><div class="stat-label">{target.season} EL NIÑO PROBABILITY</div><div class="stat-value">{target.nino}<span>%</span><span class="probability-mini"><i style={{ right: 0, width: target.nino + '%' }}></i></span></div><p>{seasonLabel(target)} · issue {snapshot.forecast.data.issue}</p></div>
    </section>
    <div class="overview-grid"><div class="main-column"><OceanMap snapshot={snapshot} /><TrendChart snapshot={snapshot} /></div><aside class="context-column"><section class="reading-section"><span class="eyebrow">THE SHORT READ</span><h2>The signal is only<br />part of the story.</h2><p>Tropical Pacific sea temperatures can shift seasonal weather patterns. They do not determine the weather in your city.</p><div class="takeaway"><span class="number">01</span><div><h3>Start with the official status</h3><p>A weekly temperature reading alone does not establish an ENSO phase.</p></div></div><div class="takeaway"><span class="number">02</span><div><h3>Read probabilities, not promises</h3><p>Seasonal odds describe uncertainty, not a guaranteed outcome.</p></div></div><a class="text-link" href="/methodology/">Understand the indicators <ArrowRight size={15} /></a></section><section class="update-section"><div class="update-icon"><CalendarDays size={20} /></div><div><span class="eyebrow">OFFICIAL UPDATES</span><h3>Follow the next CPC release</h3><p>Next scheduled discussion: {formatDate(discussion.next)}.</p><a href="https://www.cpc.ncep.noaa.gov/products/analysis_monitoring/enso_advisory/ensodisc.shtml" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">CPC release schedule <ArrowUpRight size={14} /></a></div></section></aside></div>
    <ForecastChart snapshot={snapshot} />
    <section class="impact-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">FROM SIGNAL TO SEASON</span><h2>What could it mean closer to home?</h2></div><span class="muted small">Context, not a local forecast.</span></div><div class="impact-grid"><a class="impact-item" href="/winter-outlook/"><div class="impact-icon winter-icon"><Waves size={25} /></div><div><span class="eyebrow">NORTH AMERICA</span><h3>The U.S. winter outlook</h3><p>Separate the official outlook from historical ENSO tendencies.</p></div><ArrowUpRight size={19} /></a><a class="impact-item" href="/hurricane-connection/"><div class="impact-icon hurricane-icon"><Activity size={25} /></div><div><span class="eyebrow">ATLANTIC BASIN</span><h3>The hurricane connection</h3><p>How Pacific conditions can influence Atlantic wind shear.</p></div><ArrowUpRight size={19} /></a></div></section>
    <div class="provenance-line"><span><Check size={14} /> Sources made visible</span><p>Official NOAA / CPC data. Each series retains its own observation period and source issue.</p><a href="/methodology/">Data notes <ArrowUpRight size={13} /></a></div>
  </div>
  <script>import { initCharts } from '../scripts/charts'; initCharts();</script>
</Layout>
